  "state": "closed",
  "scope": "Close the reusable software gaps identified in the algebra/device synthesis without duplicating existing QET, passivity, identifiability, archived atlas certificates, or the independent hardware-residuals analysis. Completion covers implementation and local validation, not provider acquisition, physical discoveries, hosted review, or merge.",
  "owner": "measurement-observability implementation",
  "reconciliation": {
    "status": "verified",
    "note": "The source audit distinguishes existing implementations and archived certificates from the missing reusable APIs. Analytic fixtures carry explicit observation laws and never enter the measured research ledger."
  },
  "disposition": "completed",
  "resolution": "The bounded implementation provides three Python modules, five offline analysis kinds, full native score covariance, 163 new Python tests, 25 existing counter regressions, 13 Rust tests, and passing scoped lint/type checks. Physical data collection and repository review remain separate obligations.",
